# Read-only V5 source findings

No source blocker found in the reviewed cache/admission/counter scope. Target
OpenVCL allocation/scheduling, actual output and raster remain unverified.

The arm-independent cold predicate admits only typed producer-owned original
arrays, aligned six-occurrence windows, unstripped unlit TC classification with
precise/full checks, 16-bit depth and count <=72. It rejects pool-table layouts,
directional lighting bags, billboards and custom shader overrides. The request is
then exactly enabled && eligible. Fog and selected spot contribution are allowed;
the original three fog/light paths finish all six outputs before reduction.

Both retained and baked keys include typed-owner presence, arm, fog-off and
shader-unlit facts in unused higher primKey bits. Original model/array/version
keys remain. Typed owner lives in persistent producer batch storage and is
refreshed to current arrays before render. The candidate extra primitive tag is
inline owned packet data, not a reference to a stack object. Count72 leaves
room within the existing 461-qword bank: original inputs, extra tag, maximum
nine material/primitive tags and all original outputs occupy 444 qwords.

The post-loop check visits six corners before rewriting any original output.
Packed RGBA integers, 16-bit-mode depth and fog word are exactly representable
in float for its equality tests. It compares the final Z/F/ADC word and Q, bounds
Q and rectangle differences, rejects ADC, validates rectangle orientation and
preserves original endpoint payload and material state. Shader scheduling/MAC
flag correctness still requires native review; source intent alone cannot accept
the kernel.

CoronaCounter resets/observes only at sparse epochs 750/1155, outside priced
windows. Its nine uint32 fields count cold requests and input quantities. Off
can be eligible while requested=0; fallback means EE admission failure. Retained,
baked, clipped and copied paths can bypass these counters, so zero cold requests
does not prove zero emitted SPRITE. The log explicitly sets acceptedOutputKnown=0
and README preserves this limitation. Positive requests likewise do not prove
the VU reduction passed. FogOn/shaderLit are observations, not admission cuts.

This isolated V5 fixture keeps pool2 on in kind9 and does not include lattice;
it must not be presented as cumulative #5+#4 occupancy or performance.
